<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>ExTauri — Build native desktop apps with Phoenix &amp; Elixir</title>
<meta name="description" content="ExTauri wraps Tauri so your Phoenix LiveView app runs as a native desktop application on macOS, Windows, and Linux — desktop APIs from Elixir, no JavaScript required.">
<meta property="og:title" content="ExTauri — Build native desktop apps with Phoenix &amp; Elixir">
<meta property="og:description" content="Turn your Phoenix LiveView app into a native desktop application. Notifications, dialogs, tray, filesystem and more — driven from Elixir.">
<meta property="og:type" content="website">
<link rel="icon" href="data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'%3E%3Ccircle cx='50' cy='50' r='42' fill='%238b5cf6'/%3E%3Ccircle cx='50' cy='50' r='18' fill='%23ffc131'/%3E%3C/svg%3E">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="<%= static_path("css/site.css") %>">
</head>
<body>

<nav>
  <div class="wrap nav-inner">
    <a class="logo" href="#"><span class="logo-mark"></span>ExTauri</a>
    <div class="nav-links">
      <a href="#features">Features</a>
      <a href="#get-started">Get Started</a>
      <a href="#apis">Desktop APIs</a>
      <a href="#architecture">Architecture</a>
      <a class="gh-btn" href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16"><path d="M8 0C3.58 0 0 3.58 0 8c0 3.54 2.29 6.53 5.47 7.59.4.07.55-.17.55-.38 0-.19-.01-.82-.01-1.49-2.01.37-2.53-.49-2.69-.94-.09-.23-.48-.94-.82-1.13-.28-.15-.68-.52-.01-.53.63-.01 1.08.58 1.23.82.72 1.21 1.87.87 2.33.66.07-.52.28-.87.51-1.07-1.78-.2-3.64-.89-3.64-3.95 0-.87.31-1.59.82-2.15-.08-.2-.36-1.02.08-2.12 0 0 .67-.21 2.2.82.64-.18 1.32-.27 2-.27s1.36.09 2 .27c1.53-1.04 2.2-.82 2.2-.82.44 1.1.16 1.92.08 2.12.51.56.82 1.27.82 2.15 0 3.07-1.87 3.75-3.65 3.95.29.25.54.73.54 1.48 0 1.07-.01 1.93-.01 2.2 0 .21.15.46.55.38A8.01 8.01 0 0 0 16 8c0-4.42-3.58-8-8-8z"/></svg>
        GitHub
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</nav>

<header class="hero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Build native desktop apps<br>with <span class="grad">Phoenix &amp; Elixir</span></h1>
    <p class="lede">Run your Phoenix LiveView app as a native desktop application on <strong>macOS, Windows, and Linux</strong> — desktop APIs included, no JavaScript required.</p>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#get-started">Get Started</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <div class="install-pill">
      <span class="dollar">$</span><code id="install-cmd">mix ex_tauri.install</code>
      <button class="copy-btn" data-copy="mix ex_tauri.install" title="Copy to clipboard" aria-label="Copy install command">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="hero-shot">
      <div class="titlebar"><span class="dot r"></span><span class="dot y"></span><span class="dot g"></span><span>My Phoenix App — native window</span></div>
      <img src="<%= static_path("images/example.gif") %>" alt="A Phoenix LiveView application running inside a native desktop window via ExTauri" loading="lazy">
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<section id="features">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head center">
      <div class="eyebrow">Features</div>
      <h2>Keep writing Phoenix. Ship a desktop app.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="feat-grid">
      <div class="feat"><div class="icon">🖥️</div><h3>LiveView as a Desktop App</h3><p>Your app renders inside a native window — same code, same components.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="icon">🧩</div><h3>Desktop APIs from Elixir</h3><p>Notifications, dialogs, clipboard, filesystem, tray — with callback-style responses.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="icon">🔥</div><h3>True Hot Reload</h3><p><code>mix ex_tauri.dev</code> runs your dev server inside the native window.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="icon">📡</div><h3>Server-Side Channel</h3><p>Send notifications and drive the system tray from GenServers — no browser involved.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="icon">📦</div><h3>Single Binary</h3><p>Burrito bundles the BEAM and your app into one executable per platform.</p></div>
      <div class="feat"><div class="icon">💓</div><h3>Graceful Shutdown</h3><p>Heartbeat-based cleanup, even on force-quit or crash.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="get-started" class="alt">
  <div class="wrap narrow">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Get Started</div>
      <h2>Three steps to a native window</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <div><div class="step-num">1</div></div>
        <div>
          <h3>Add the dependency</h3>
          <div class="code"><div class="code-label"><span>mix.exs</span></div><pre><code class="lang-elixir">{:ex_tauri, git: "https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri.git"}</code></pre></div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <div><div class="step-num">2</div></div>
        <div>
          <h3>Install</h3>
          <div class="code"><div class="code-label"><span>shell</span></div><pre><code class="lang-bash">mix deps.get
mix ex_tauri.install</code></pre></div>
          <p class="step-note">One command wires everything: config, Rust scaffolding, supervision tree, JS hook, and layout.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="step">
        <div><div class="step-num">3</div></div>
        <div>
          <h3>Run it</h3>
          <div class="code"><div class="code-label"><span>shell</span></div><pre><code class="lang-bash">mix ex_tauri.dev</code></pre></div>
          <p class="step-note">Your app opens in a native window with code reloading and live reload, exactly as in the browser.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="prereqs">Requires Elixir ≥ 1.15 with OTP 27, <a href="https://www.rust-lang.org/tools/install">Rust</a>, and the <a href="https://v2.tauri.app/start/prerequisites/">Tauri prerequisites</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="apis">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Desktop APIs</div>
      <h2>Native capabilities, idiomatic Elixir</h2>
      <p>Add <code class="inline">use ExTauri.LiveView</code> and every API accepts a callback that receives the result — no manual event pattern-matching.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tabs" role="tablist">
      <button class="tab active" data-tab="dialog">📂 File Dialogs</button>
      <button class="tab" data-tab="notify">🔔 Notifications</button>
      <button class="tab" data-tab="events">🎯 Native Events</button>
      <button class="tab" data-tab="desktop">📡 Server-Side Tray</button>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-panel active" data-panel="dialog">
      <div class="code"><div class="code-label"><span>lib/my_app_web/live/home_live.ex</span></div><pre><code class="lang-elixir">defmodule MyAppWeb.HomeLive do
  use MyAppWeb, :live_view
  use ExTauri.LiveView

  def handle_event("pick_file", _params, socket) do
    socket =
      ExTauri.Dialog.open(socket, [title: "Pick a file"], fn
        {:ok, %{"path" => path}}, socket -> assign(socket, :file, path)
        {:error, _reason}, socket -> put_flash(socket, :error, "No file selected")
      end)

    {:noreply, socket}
  end
end</code></pre></div>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-panel" data-panel="notify">
      <div class="code"><div class="code-label"><span>lib/my_app_web/live/home_live.ex</span></div><pre><code class="lang-elixir">def handle_event("notify", _params, socket) do
  socket = ExTauri.Notification.send(socket, "Saved!", body: "Your file was saved.")
  {:noreply, socket}
end</code></pre></div>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-panel" data-panel="events">
      <div class="code"><div class="code-label"><span>lib/my_app_web/live/editor_live.ex</span></div><pre><code class="lang-elixir">def mount(_params, _session, socket) do
  {:ok, ExTauri.Event.subscribe(socket, "tauri://drag-drop")}
end

# React to files dropped onto the window
def handle_event("tauri_event", %{"payload" => %{"paths" => paths}}, socket) do
  {:noreply, assign(socket, :dropped_files, paths)}
end</code></pre></div>
    </div>

    <div class="tab-panel" data-panel="desktop">
      <div class="code"><div class="code-label"><span>anywhere in your app — no LiveView needed</span></div><pre><code class="lang-elixir"># Notify from a background job
ExTauri.Desktop.notify("Sync complete", body: "128 records updated")

# Define a system tray from Elixir; clicks arrive as messages
ExTauri.Desktop.set_tray(
  tooltip: "My App",
  items: [%{id: "sync", label: "Sync now"}, %{id: "quit", label: "Quit"}]
)</code></pre></div>
    </div>

    <p class="api-note"><b>Notification, Shell, Window, Event, App</b> and <b>Desktop</b> work out of the box. Dialogs, clipboard, filesystem, global shortcuts, autostart, updater, and deep links are one <code class="inline">mix ex_tauri.add &lt;plugin&gt;</code> away — see the <a href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri#using-desktop-apis">full list</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="architecture" class="alt">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="sec-head">
      <div class="eyebrow">Architecture</div>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="arch-grid">
      <div class="arch-diagram">
        <div class="arch-box tauri">
          <b>🪟 Tauri Window</b>
          <span>Native window · Rust / WebView</span>
          <div class="arch-inner">Phoenix UI — your LiveView app rendered in the WebView</div>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-link">
          <span class="pipe">│</span>
          <span><b>HTTP</b> — serves your Phoenix UI to the WebView</span>
          <span><b>Local socket</b> — heartbeat + desktop channel</span>
          <span class="pipe">│</span>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-box phoenix">
          <b>🐦‍🔥 Phoenix Server</b>
          <span>Your Elixir app · Burrito-wrapped sidecar process</span>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="arch-list">
        <div class="arch-item">
          <h4>A sidecar, not a rewrite</h4>
          <p>Tauri launches your Phoenix app as a sidecar process on an OS-assigned free port and navigates the window once the server is up. Standard <code class="inline">runtime.exs</code> conventions apply.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="arch-item">
          <h4>Crash-safe shutdown</h4>
          <p>The frontend heartbeats over a local socket; if it stops — quit, crash, or force-kill — Phoenix shuts down cleanly. Works on every platform, including Windows.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="ship">
  <div class="wrap narrow center-text">
    <div class="sec-head center">
      <div class="eyebrow">Ship It</div>
      <h2>One command to production bundles</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="code ship-code"><div class="code-label"><span>shell</span></div><pre><code class="lang-bash">mix ex_tauri.build</code></pre></div>
    <ul class="bundle-row">
      <li>🍎 macOS <span class="fmt">.app · .dmg</span></li>
      <li>🐧 Linux <span class="fmt">.deb · .appimage</span></li>
      <li>🪟 Windows <span class="fmt">.msi · .exe</span></li>
    </ul>
    <p class="prereqs">Signing, notarization, auto-updates, CI matrix: <a href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri/blob/main/guides/releasing.md">release guide</a>. Working demos in <a href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri/tree/main/demos">demos/</a> and <a href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri/tree/main/example">example/</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<div class="final-cta">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2>Your LiveView app, <span class="grad">on the desktop</span></h2>
    <div class="cta-row">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#get-started">Get Started</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri">Star on GitHub ★</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<footer>
  <div class="wrap foot-inner">
    <div>ExTauri · MIT License · © <%= @year %> · Built with ❤️ on the BEAM, served by <a href="https://francis.build">Francis</a></div>
    <div class="links">
      <a href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri">GitHub</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/filipecabaco/ex_tauri/blob/main/guides/releasing.md">Release Guide</a>
      <a href="https://tauri.app">Tauri</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/burrito-elixir/burrito">Burrito</a>
      <a href="https://francis.build">Francis</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</footer>

<script src="<%= static_path("js/site.js") %>" defer></script>
</body>
</html>
